# Secrets. The Admin API token is a full write credential for the live store -
# it must never reach the repo, which is pushed to GitHub.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.token
secrets.json

# Shopify CLI
.shopify/
*.lock

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Agent skills installed by `npx skills add`. These are local dev tooling, not
# theme files, and this repo is GitHub-synced straight into the ka_cc/redesign
# theme - anything committed here lands on the store. A Shopify theme only
# accepts a fixed set of top-level directories, so these would be junk at best
# and a sync error at worst. .shopifyignore doesn't help: the GitHub
# integration ignores it and syncs whatever is committed.
.agents/
.claude/
skills-lock.json

# Camera originals for the site photography (~92MB of full-size JPEG/HEIC).
# The web-sized copies that the theme actually serves are committed in
# assets/ as kcc-*.jpg; keeping the masters out stops the repo ballooning.
# They stay on disk so photos can be re-cropped or re-exported later.
KCC Website Photos/
.taste-skill/

# Master artwork for the ingredient-section backdrop (4.3MB Affinity export).
# assets/ingredient-scatter.svg is the committed, theme-sized derivative;
# regenerate it with scripts/build-ingredient-scatter.py when the drawing
# changes. Same reasoning as the photo masters above - and here it matters
# twice over, since a stray 4.3MB file at the theme root is not a directory
# Shopify accepts.
KCC All.svg

# Master artwork for the nine ingredient drawings (12.5MB Affinity export).
# snippets/ingredient-icon-sprite.liquid holds the committed, theme-sized
# derivative. Same reasoning as KCC All.svg above: at the theme root this
# would be both a sync error and 12MB of dead weight on the store.
KCC Website Aromatics.svg

# Master for the why-ka letterform backdrop (5.4MB, cream on black).
# assets/ka-pattern.png is the committed alpha-mask derivative; rebuild it
# with scripts/build-ka-pattern.py. Same reasoning as the artwork above.
KCC Ka Pattern.png
